            "In Appendix~\\ref{app:which-tasks-helpful}, we include ablations that provide more insights on the choice of meta-training tasks, such as (1) high quality data with diverse domains tend to help (e.g., GLUE family~\\citep{wang2018glue}) and (2) adversarially collected data tends to be unhelpful. However, more systematic studies on how to choose the best meta-training tasks and how they relate to particular target tasks should be done, which we leave for future work.\n",
            "\n",
